      <text:p text:style-name="P55">Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure5" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">6</text:sequence>: Cell D Subscribes to Cell E in Domain D<text:span text:style-name="T218">2</text:span></text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T229">A</text:span>nother way would be if cell F were interested in stimuli from cell E in domain D<text:span text:style-name="T218">2</text:span>. <text:s/>A stimulus would travel through cell D on its way to cell F. <text:s/>Cell D would then find the subscription for cell E stimuli in domain D<text:span text:style-name="T218">1</text:span> and forward the stimulus.</text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"/>
