      <text:p text:style-name="P55">Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure10" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">11</text:sequence>: WorldHello <text:span text:style-name="T372">System</text:span> Model</text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame><text:soft-page-break/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">If we imagine that <text:span text:style-name="T304">f</text:span>igure <text:span text:style-name="T325">1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T343">1</text:span> represents a broadcast of the hail, then <text:span text:style-name="T304">f</text:span>igure <text:span text:style-name="T325">1</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T343">2</text:span> might represent a courier physically delivering the hail to each city. <text:s/><text:span text:style-name="T185">In this model, a hail would traverse the entire </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T372">system</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T185">, and each salutation would take a journey as well.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P22"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Frame6" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:x="0.8902in" svg:y="0.0799in" svg:width="4.7945in" draw:z-index="16">
